## 1. Ticket At A Glance

When the `agentic-hq` CLI is run from a directory whose **local workspace** defines a workflow with
the same short name as one shipped in the **AHQ package**, the CLI crashes during program
construction with an uncaught Commander error — *before any subcommand runs*:

```
Error: cannot add command 'add-feature' as already have command 'add-feature'
```

Every invocation from such a directory fails: `list`, `add-feature`, `--help`, and a bare
`agentic-hq`. Exit code 1. There is no workaround other than changing directory or renaming the
local workflow.

**Expected behaviour (per the Jira):** a *deliberate collision policy* instead of a crash. The Jira
offers three candidate behaviours and explicitly says a **decision is needed** — see §6.

