## 3. Reproduction — Confirmed, Four Ways

All four were run on 2026-08-16 on this machine (macOS, Node v24.15.0, `agentic-hq` working tree at
`feature/ahq-195-publish-to-npm`, commit `b959e2f`). Fixtures live in `temp/AHQ-205/` (gitignored).

### 3.1 The real scenario — prebuilt package run from the repo clone root ✅ reproduced

This is the exact structural equivalent of the reported npm-install case: the prebuilt artifact in
`release/` *is* the installed package (`--ahq-package-root=<repo>/release`), and the cwd is the repo
clone, whose local workspace ships `add-feature`.

```bash
cd /Users/stevepersonal/dev/agentic-hq/agentic-hq
node release/bin/agentic-hq-prebuilt.cjs list
```

Produces the **line-for-line stack trace from the Jira**, through the compiled `release/dist/…`
files: `WorkflowRegistryImpl.register` → `PluginImpl.registerWorkflowsWith` →
`WorkspaceImpl.registerWorkflowsWith` → `CurrentUserWorkspaceImpl.registerWorkflowsWith` →
`WorkflowSearchResultsImpl.registerWorkflowsWith` → `createProgram`.

### 3.2 Minimal synthetic repro — dev wrapper, colliding local workflow ✅ reproduced

No build or install needed. A local workspace containing one workflow whose `shortId` is
`add-feature`, under a plugin named something else entirely:

```
temp/AHQ-205/repro-workspace/.agentic-hq/plugins/my-local-plugin/skills/add-feature/ahq-workflow.json
  { "pluginId": "my-local-plugin", "skillId": "add-feature", "shortId": "add-feature", … }
```

```bash
cd temp/AHQ-205/repro-workspace
node /path/to/agentic-hq/bin/agentic-hq.cjs list
```

Same error, same chain (through `src/…` rather than `dist/…`). **Every** entry point crashes —
verified individually: `list`, `add-feature --help`, `--help`, `math`, and bare `agentic-hq`, all
exit code **1**.

This matters for the fix: the collision needs **only a matching `shortId`**. The plugin names do not
have to match, so this is not a "don't clone the repo" problem — it is any user whose project
defines a workflow called `add-feature` or `math`.

### 3.3 Undiscovered variant — two plugins in **one** workspace ✅ reproduced

Not mentioned in the Jira. Two plugins in the *same* workspace, each with `shortId: "dup"`:

```
Error: cannot add command 'dup' as already have command 'dup'
```

The cross-workspace dedup guard (`isAhqPackage()`) is irrelevant here — this crashes even in a
single workspace, and it crashes inside the **AHQ package itself** if two shipped plugins ever
collide. Any fix scoped only to "local vs package" leaves this crash in place.

### 3.4 Undiscovered variant — a workflow named `list` ✅ reproduced

Also not in the Jira. A workflow whose `shortId` is `list` collides with the CLI's own built-in
subcommand (`agentic-hq-program.ts:41`):

```
Error: cannot add command 'list' as already have command 'list'
```

This is the nastiest of the four, because `list` is the very command a confused user would run to
find out what is going on.

**Checked and clear:** `help` is **not** reserved. A workflow with `shortId: "help"` registers
cleanly and appears in `--help` output — Commander's implicit help is not a registered command, so
it does not collide. `list` is the only reserved name today (verified, not assumed).

