## 5. Research Findings

### 5.1 The collision key is `shortId` alone

`WorkflowRegistryImpl.register` uses `workflow.getShortName()` as the Commander command name.
`shortId` comes straight from each `ahq-workflow.json`. Current shipped short names:

| shortId | Plugin / skill |
| --- | --- |
| `create-workflow` | `agentic-hq-core-plugin/skills/create-workflow` |
| `add-feature` | `agentic-hq-demos-plugin/skills/add-feature` |
| `add-feature-detailed-example` | `agentic-hq-demos-plugin/skills/add-feature-detailed-example` |
| `full-jira` | `agentic-hq-demos-plugin/skills/full-jira-tdd-story-workflow` |
| `math` | `agentic-hq-demos-plugin/skills/math-workflow` |
| `quick-jira` | `agentic-hq-demos-plugin/skills/quick-jira-workflow` |
| `reversal` | `agentic-hq-demos-plugin/skills/string-reversal` |

Only **`add-feature`** and **`math`** currently ship in the published artifact (the other five are in
`EXCLUDED_UNMIGRATED_SKILLS` in `scripts/build-release.cjs` until AHQ-201) — so those two, plus the
built-in `list`, are the live minefield for npm users today. After AHQ-201 all seven become live.

### 5.2 ⚠️ Claude Code silently de-duplicates same-named plugins — **first `--plugin-dir` wins**

This is the most consequential finding, and it constrains the fix. Empirically probed on 2026-08-16
with two directories both containing a plugin manifest named `dupe-probe-plugin`, each exposing a
skill `probe-skill` with a distinguishable description:

```bash
claude --plugin-dir=…/a/dupe-probe-plugin --plugin-dir=…/b/dupe-probe-plugin --print …
#  → "one probe-skill entry: dupe-probe-plugin:probe-skill — 'Probe skill copy a'"

claude --plugin-dir=…/b/dupe-probe-plugin --plugin-dir=…/a/dupe-probe-plugin --print …
#  → "one probe-skill entry: dupe-probe-plugin:probe-skill — 'Probe skill copy b'"
```

So Claude Code accepts the duplicate without error, exposes exactly **one** copy, and the **first
flag wins**. And `ClaudeCommandBuilder.getClaudeCliPluginDirArgs()`
(`src/tools/marshalled-io-tools/claude-code/claude-command-builder.ts:118-131`) adds the **AHQ
package's** plugin dirs first, the user's second.

**Consequence:** the collision has two sub-cases which behave differently below the CLI layer.

- **Different plugin names** (e.g. `my-local-plugin:add-feature` vs
  `agentic-hq-demos-plugin:add-feature`). The two workflows produce *different*
  `/pluginId:skillId` commands, so whichever one the CLI registers is genuinely the one that runs.
  A "local wins" policy is honest here.
- **Same plugin name** — which is exactly the reported repo-clone case, where both roots contain
  `agentic-hq-demos-plugin`. Both workflows produce the *identical* command
  `/agentic-hq-demos-plugin:add-feature`, and Claude resolves it to the **AHQ package's** copy
  because that `--plugin-dir` came first. A "local wins" policy implemented only in the Commander
  registry would therefore **announce local and silently run the package's copy**.

Any precedence policy must therefore be applied in **both** places — the workflow registry *and* the
`--plugin-dir` ordering — or it is a lie. This is a genuine second defect hiding behind the first,
and it is invisible today only because the crash happens first.

### 5.3 Discovery is cwd-only, never ancestor-walking

`CurrentUserWorkspaceImpl.createDelegate()` uses `process.cwd()` and nothing else. Verified: running
the prebuilt wrapper from `<repo>/src` lists normally, because `src/` has no `.agentic-hq/plugins/`.
Only a directory that *itself* contains `.agentic-hq/plugins/` participates. This bounds the blast
radius and means no fix needs to consider parent directories.

### 5.4 The listing has the same problem, one layer up

`ListingFormatter` renders the AHQ package block and the local workspace block independently
(`listing-formatter.ts:55-95`). With registration fixed but the formatter untouched, `agentic-hq
list` would print two identical-looking `agentic-hq add-feature` entries with no hint that only one
of them is reachable. The listing is where a user goes to understand the situation, so it has to
show the outcome, not just the inventory.

### 5.5 Path normalisation — one of the two flagged cases is real

`WorkspaceImpl.isAhqPackage()` (`workspace-impl.ts:76-78`) is raw string equality. Both flagged
cases were tested:

- **Symlinked invocation — not a defect.** Running via a symlink to the repo root
  (`cd temp/AHQ-205/repo-symlink && node bin/agentic-hq.cjs list`) works correctly. Both
  `process.cwd()` and CJS `__dirname` resolve to physical paths on this platform, so the two sides
  of the comparison agree. No normalisation needed for this.
- **Trailing slash — a real miss.** Passing the option by hand with a trailing separator
  (`--ahq-package-root=/Users/…/agentic-hq/`) makes `isAhqPackage()` return `false` while standing
  in the package root, so the package's own plugins register twice and the CLI crashes
  (`cannot add command 'create-workflow' …`). Both shipped bin wrappers build the value with
  `path.join(__dirname, '..')`, which never yields a trailing slash — so this is **not** reachable
  through normal use, only through a hand-written invocation or a future third entry point.

Verdict for the explicit decision the brief asked for: normalise, but treat it as **defence in
depth, not the fix**. Normalising the comparison (e.g. `path.resolve` on both sides) is a two-line
change that removes a whole class of "silently miss" bugs, and once the name-collision policy exists
a missed guard degrades into "duplicate name handled by policy" instead of a crash.

### 5.6 The crash is at construction, so nothing can catch it usefully

`app.run()` (`src/cli/app.ts:25-28`) builds the program and parses in one expression. The throw
happens inside `createProgram`, so Commander never sees argv — which is why even `--help` dies. Any
fix must prevent the duplicate registration rather than handle a failure after it.

### 5.7 AHQ-200's `ahq-package-root` rename — static verification done

Verified in the working tree today: the add-feature CLI broadcasts the new name
(`.../skills/add-feature/ts-workflow/src/add-feature-cli.ts:55` →
`` `…ahq-package-root=${runtime.getAhqPackageRoot().getPath()}` ``), the SKILL.md relays it
(`SKILL.md:12,22`), and **all four** command parsers (`commands/add-feature/01-researcher.md`,
`02-planner.md`, `03-implementer.md`, `04-reviewer.md`) read `ahq-package-root` — with no
`agentic-hq-workspace-root-dir` remaining in any of them. The remaining half of the AHQ-200 check is
purely runtime: confirm Command 01's actual `command-input.json` carries `ahq-package-root=…`.

